  "table_html": "\n\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <h2>Worked example - feature #25</h2>\n  <p>The feature that moved the most among the reliable ones, at $\\mathbf u = (243,\\ 911)$\n    in frame $t$. The window is 21 &times; 21 pixels and the pyramid has\n    4 levels. Gradients $I_x, I_y$ come from the Scharr filter divided by 32, in grey levels per pixel.</p>\n\n  <h3>1. Structure tensor at level 0</h3>\n  <div class=\"theory-block\">\n    $$ G = \\sum_W \\begin{bmatrix} I_x^2 & I_xI_y \\\\ I_xI_y & I_y^2 \\end{bmatrix}\n         = \\begin{bmatrix} 6142.3 & 1099.4 \\\\ 1099.4 & 10576.1 \\end{bmatrix},\n       \\qquad \\lambda_1 = 10833.7,\\ \\ \\lambda_2 = 5884.7 $$\n  </div>\n  <p>Both eigenvalues are large (per window pixel $\\lambda_2 / 441 = 13.3$,\n    and the threshold is 0.01). The ratio is $\\lambda_1/\\lambda_2 = 1.84$, so this is a\n    corner and not an edge, and $G$ is safely invertible.</p>\n\n  <h3>2. Iterations at level 0</h3>\n  <p>The coarser pyramid levels hand down the initial guess\n    $\\mathbf g^0 = (-5.815,\\ 2.628)$. Each row solves\n    $G\\boldsymbol\\delta = \\mathbf b_k$ with $\\mathbf b_k = \\sum_W \\big(I(\\mathbf x) - J(\\mathbf x + \\mathbf d_k)\\big)\\,[I_x, I_y]^{\\mathsf T}$,\n    where $J$ is sampled with bilinear interpolation.</p>\n  <table class=\"result-table\">\n    <tr><th>k</th><th>$\\mathbf d_k$ (x, y)</th><th>$\\mathbf b_k$</th><th>$\\boldsymbol\\delta = G^{-1}\\mathbf b_k$</th><th>$|\\boldsymbol\\delta|$</th><th>RMS $I - J$</th></tr>\n    \n    <tr><td>0</td>\n      <td>(-5.8152, 2.6279)</td>\n      <td>(-430.5, 203.9)</td>\n      <td>(-0.0749, +0.0271)</td>\n      <td>0.0797</td>\n      <td>1.19</td></tr>\n    \n    <tr><td>1</td>\n      <td>(-5.8902, 2.6550)</td>\n      <td>(-0.0, -35.7)</td>\n      <td>(+0.0006, -0.0034)</td>\n      <td>0.0035</td>\n      <td>1.12</td></tr>\n    \n  </table>\n  <p class=\"muted\">The iteration stops when $|\\boldsymbol\\delta| < 0.01$ px. This one converged in 2 step(s).</p>\n\n  <h3>3. Prediction vs. actual</h3>\n  <div class=\"theory-block\">\n    $$ \\mathbf u' = \\mathbf u + \\mathbf d = (243,\\ 911) + (-5.890,\\ 2.652)\n       = (237.110,\\ 913.652) $$\n    $$ \\text{actual (NCC peak)} = (237.019,\\ 913.689), \\qquad\n       \\lVert \\mathbf u' - \\mathbf u'_{\\text{actual}} \\rVert = 0.098\\ \\text{px} $$\n    $$ \\text{OpenCV LK: } \\mathbf d = (-5.889,\\ 2.652), \\qquad\n       \\text{difference from ours} = 0.0001\\ \\text{px} $$\n  </div>\n  <p>Brightness constancy check: the mean $|I(\\mathbf x) - J(\\mathbf x + \\mathbf d)|$ over the window drops from\n    10.98 grey levels at $\\mathbf d = \\mathbf 0$ to 0.78 at the tracked $\\mathbf d$.</p>\n\n  <h3>4. Bilinear interpolation at the tracked position</h3>\n  <p>The centre of the window lands at $(x, y) = (237.1105,\\ 913.6515)$ in frame $t+1$, so\n    $x_0 = 237$, $y_0 = 913$, $a = 0.1105$, $b = 0.6515$. The four neighbours are:</p>\n  <div class=\"theory-block\">\n    $$ \\begin{bmatrix} f_{00} & f_{10} \\\\ f_{01} & f_{11} \\end{bmatrix}\n       = \\begin{bmatrix} 140 & 121 \\\\ 134 & 128 \\end{bmatrix} $$\n    $$ f(x, y_0) = (1-a)f_{00} + a f_{10} = 0.8895\\cdot140 + 0.1105\\cdot121 = 137.9014 $$\n    $$ f(x, y_0{+}1) = (1-a)f_{01} + a f_{11} = 0.8895\\cdot134 + 0.1105\\cdot128 = 133.3373 $$\n    $$ f(x, y) = (1-b)\\,137.9014 + b\\,133.3373 = 134.9278 $$\n  </div>\n  <p>Equivalently, the weights $(1-a)(1-b), a(1-b), (1-a)b, ab$ are\n    0.3100, 0.0385, 0.5796, 0.0720\n    (sum 1.0000). OpenCV's <code>getRectSubPix</code> at the same point gives\n    134.9279 (difference 8.2e-05, which is float32 rounding).\n    For comparison, the pixel at $\\mathbf u$ in frame $t$ is 130: the interpolated\n    value in frame $t+1$ is close to it, as brightness constancy says it should be.</p>\n</div>\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"card\">\n  <h2>Every tracked feature</h2>\n  <p class=\"muted\">All positions in pixels. \"Actual\" is the NCC template-match location in frame t+1. Grey rows\n    have a weak match (NCC &le; 0.9, e.g. on a motion boundary or in repeated texture) and are left out of the statistics.</p>\n  <div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\">\n  <table class=\"result-table\">\n    <tr><th>#</th><th>u (frame t)</th><th>d (our LK)</th><th>predicted u + d</th><th>actual</th><th>error</th>\n      <th>d (OpenCV)</th><th>NCC</th><th>$\\lambda_2$/px</th><th>residual</th></tr>\n    \n    <tr >\n      <td>1</td><td>(15, 175)</td>\n      <td>(-0.615, -0.326)</td>\n      <td>(14.38, 174.67)</td>\n      <td>(14.31, 174.70)</td>\n      <td>0.076</td>\n      <td>(-0.613, -0.325)</td>\n      <td>0.900</td>\n      <td>430.4</td>\n      <td>16.8 &rarr; 9.4</td>\n    </tr>\n    \n    <tr >\n      <td>2</td><td>(30, 172)</td>\n      <td>(-0.659, -0.371)</td>\n      <td>(29.34, 171.63)</td>\n      <td>(29.63, 172.12)</td>\n      <td>0.569</td>\n      <td>(-0.659, -0.371)</td>\n      <td>0.947</td>\n      <td>68.1</td>\n      <td>4.6 &rarr; 3.3</td>\n    </tr>\n    \n    <tr >\n      <td>3</td><td>(23, 134)</td>\n      <td>(-0.699, -0.374)</td>\n      <td>(22.30, 133.63)</td>\n      <td>(22.27, 133.66)</td>\n      <td>0.045</td>\n      <td>(-0.699, -0.374)</td>\n      <td>0.923</td>\n      <td>232.8</td>\n      <td>11.4 &rarr; 5.7</td>\n    </tr>\n    \n    <tr >\n      <td>4</td><td>(31, 154)</td>\n      <td>(-0.694, -0.393)</td>\n      <td>(30.31, 153.61)</td>\n      <td>(30.35, 153.54)</td>\n      <td>0.077</td>\n      <td>(-0.694, -0.393)</td>\n      <td>0.922</td>\n      <td>194.5</td>\n      <td>11.5 &rarr; 5.5</td>\n    </tr>\n    \n    <tr >\n      <td>5</td><td>(19, 163)</td>\n      <td>(-0.663, -0.369)</td>\n      <td>(18.34, 162.63)</td>\n      <td>(18.28, 162.65)</td>\n      <td>0.058</td>\n      <td>(-0.663, -0.369)</td>\n      <td>0.914</td>\n      <td>417.1</td>\n      <td>19.5 &rarr; 8.3</td>\n    </tr>\n    \n    <tr style=\"opacity:.5\">\n      <td>6</td><td>(34, 258)</td>\n      <td>(-0.599, -0.296)</td>\n      <td>(33.40, 257.70)</td>\n      <td>(33.45, 2